<urn:atm:triage:finding/AY9-QA-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AY9-QA-001" ;
  triage:title "boundaries lint fails: transport.rs calls HerdrEndpointDisplay::from_relative outside its sole permitted composition root, boundaries/atm-core/herdr-endpoint-doctor.toml not updated for the AY.9 C1a amendment" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr qa-pr1295-r1 (PR #1295, AY.9 herdr-socket-cutover, dedicated QA worktree pinned at ba7966c32). Live CI run 34142141660 (head ba7966c32) fails job 'Just lint (ubuntu-latest)' at the 'boundaries' check with exit code 1: crates/atm-herdr/src/transport.rs:189,200,231,247 all trip 'BOUNDARY-HerdrEndpointDoctor forbids external reference HerdrEndpointDisplay::from_relative'. boundaries/atm-core/herdr-endpoint-doctor.toml's [status].notes states 'atm_herdr::doctor_probe is recorded as a composition root because HerdrDoctorProbe is the only site permitted to call HerdrEndpointDisplay::from_relative (AY.3 C6 sanitizer); no production reference outside atm-core is permitted by this record,' and [composition].roots = ['atm_herdr::doctor_probe'] / [references].forbidden = ['HerdrEndpointDisplay::from_relative'] encode exactly that. The AY.9 sprint doc's own C1a allowlist explicitly relocated the HerdrEndpoint-to-HerdrEndpointDisplay conversion into transport.rs ('crates/atm-herdr/src/doctor_probe.rs (the one assignment/call site that hard-codes doctor transport CLI and endpoint None; added by fenix 2026-09-07 as a C1a plan defect found during AY.9 D4, arch-ctm msg 01M1Y9F78Z4Q1W4K5NHHA294AQ; conversion stays in transport.rs so HerdrEndpoint never crosses the crate)') -- so the dev correctly implemented the sprint doc's stated C1a intent, but the C1a allowlist never added boundaries/atm-core/herdr-endpoint-doctor.toml itself, so the TOML's composition-root/forbidden-reference contract was never updated to match. The CI-enforced boundary lint (.just/lint_boundaries.py, LINT-BOUNDARY-HERDR-ENDPOINT-DOCTOR-REFERENCES) therefore correctly flags the mismatch: it is enforcing a now-stale contract against code the sprint doc itself directed. This is a genuine hard CI gate failure (job conclusion=failure, not pending/flaky) at the pinned head, confirmed live via gh api jobs/101806869635/logs and the uploaded just-lint-logs-ubuntu-latest artifact's 20260907161650-boundaries.log. All other lint categories (fmt, clippy, deny, shear, arch-gates, version, adr-index, unix-gating, sc-boundary, pytests, etc.) pass at this head; locally-run cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings, cargo test -p atm-herdr --all-features (48+3+8+1 passed), cargo test -p atm-daemon-bootstrap (83 passed incl. herdr_lifecycle_tests L1-L12), and cargo test -p atm-architecture --test boundary_enforcement (95 passed incl. ay3_herdr_endpoint_doctor_contract_has_only_closed_and_bootstrap_implementations) all pass -- this is exclusively a Python-lint boundary-TOML/reality mismatch, not a Rust defect. Fix is a boundary-doc update to boundaries/atm-core/herdr-endpoint-doctor.toml: add the AY.9 composition root (transport.rs's socket_endpoint_display/configured_endpoint_display/named_pipe_display helper family, or the module atm_herdr::transport) alongside/in place of atm_herdr::doctor_probe, and update the stale [status].notes prose accordingly -- not a code change to transport.rs, which correctly implements C1a/C2's sanitizer contract (verified: from_relative call sites only ever originate from within crate-private transport.rs helpers reachable solely via HerdrIo::endpoint_display, itself only called from doctor_probe.rs; no leak of raw paths). Per repo boundary-doc governance this TOML edit needs boundary-guard review before merge, same as any other boundary-policy change." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ay" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "contract-fidelity" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "boundaries/atm-core/herdr-endpoint-doctor.toml, crates/atm-herdr/src/transport.rs" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-07T16:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AY9 ;
